        "Footnotes" : "Note: On September 30, 2022, the x-axis was changed from ‘Reporting Week’ to ‘Current Season Week Ending Date’; data for prior seasons were adjusted accordingly. Data for prior seasons with ‘Reporting Week’ as the x-axis are archived and accessible via https://data.cdc.gov/Vaccinations/Weekly-Cumulative-Doses-in-Millions-of-Influenza-V/k87d-gv3u/about_data. During influenza season 2023-2024, due to 53 weeks in the 2024 calendar year, the first data collection and reporting period spanned two weeks from January 1, 2024 through January 13, 2024. To adjust the visualization for this, the estimate for week ending January 6, 2024 and week ending January 13, 2024 is the same and represents vaccinations distributed during this two-week period. Archived data are available here: https://data.cdc.gov/resource/e5zk-7tx5.  Additional information on vaccine supply is available at https://www.cdc.gov/flu/hcp/vaccine-supply. ",
